course: dictionary
lesson: 13789
title: Inundated: flooded or overwhelmed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inundated has two meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. The first is flooded, covered with a large amount of water. «After the heavy rain, the fields were inundated and the river rose.» Water, rain and rivers are the clues here.
explain: The second meaning is overwhelmed: you have so many things, like letters, calls or jobs, that it is hard to deal with them all. «After the video went viral, Maya was inundated with messages.» Messages and too many things are the clues here, so inundated does not mean wet.
explain: Inundated is the past form of the verb inundate, so it describes something that has already happened. Look for the words that often come with it: inundated with or inundated by. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Inundated means flooded, or covered with a large amount of water.
fact: Inundated can also mean overwhelmed, having so many things that it is hard to deal with them all.
fact: Inundated is often followed by with or by, as in inundated with requests or inundated by visitors.
fact: Inundate is the verb, and inundated is its past form, as in «The shop was inundated yesterday».
fact: Overwhelmed is a close synonym for the second meaning, but inundated also suggests a huge flood of things.
exercise: «After the storm, the low fields were inundated by the river.» What does inundated mean here? | Dry and dusty | *Flooded with water | Painted bright green | Cleaned and tidy
exercise: «Ravi was inundated with emails from his club.» What does inundated mean here? | *He had so many emails it was hard to deal with them all | He lost every email in a flood | He was bored and read nothing | He had no emails to read
exercise: «The town was inundated when the river rose.» Which word near inundated tells you it means flooded? | was | *river | town
test: «Her phone was inundated with calls after the news.» What does inundated mean? | Lost in a pocket | *Overwhelmed by too many calls to deal with | Switched off for the night | Covered with paint
test: Which sentence uses inundated to mean flooded? | «The children were inundated with homework.» | «He was inundated with praise.» | «The shop was inundated with customers.» | *«The basement was inundated after the pipe burst.»
exam: How can you check the meaning of inundated in a new sentence? | Ignore the words around it | Skip the whole sentence forever | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense | Guess from the first letter only
